e burst, not its last notification. A burst is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one window as far as the merge is concerned, and “the last one wins” would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently drop every notification but one — on a debounce that exists","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precisely because bursts are expected, that is a change quietly going","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"missing rather than a visible failure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only notifications the observer ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"accepted","type":"text"}]},{"text":" are represented. A notification","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a store the observer was told it doesn’t own is dropped before it gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here; one whose store can’t be identified is always accepted, and sets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifiedStore","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Why there is no history token","anchor":"Why-there-is-no-history-token"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The underlying notification carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryTokenKey"},{"text":", and it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deliberately not surfaced. That value is a CoreData ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryToken"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the watermark in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" is a SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultHistoryToken"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose only public initializer is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"text":" — there is no supported","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion between the two, and SwiftData’s interface names no CoreData type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at all. Publishing a token that neither Swidux nor an app author can act on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be an invitation to misuse it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator.mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"text":" anchors its watermark on the last transaction in the window it just scanned, so it already holds the token it needs.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxCloudKitSync/documentation/SwiduxCloudKitSync/RemoteChange":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stores one coalesced burst of remote-change notifications named."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemoteChange"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxcloudkitsync\/remotechange","kind":"symbol","title":"RemoteChange"},"doc://SwiduxCloudKitSync/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://SwiduxCloudKitSync/documentation/SwiduxCloudKitSync":{"title":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxcloudkitsync","abstract":[],"role":"collect